    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nsurround\n\n### Description\n\n[`nvim-surround`](https://github.com/kylechui/nvim-surround) can keep the cursor position after performing a surround action. For example, consider this text:\r\n(`|` represents the cursor)\r\n```html\r\n<h1>hea|ding</h1>\r\n```\r\nAfter performing a surround action like `srtth2` the cursor moves to the beginning of the surrounded text:\r\n```html\r\n<h2>|heading</h2>\r\n```\r\nHowever if I do the same thing with `nvim-surround` the cursor position doesn't change:\r\n```html\r\n<h2>hea|ding</h2>\r\n```\r\nPlease refer to their docs for more information: https://github.com/kylechui/nvim-surround/blob/cfa2da7f469f1e759f2a961bc25fa4ccfe1795c2/doc/nvim-surround.txt#L612\r\n\r\nI find this feature very usefull. Specially, when performing a surround action on multiple lines, the jump is quite distracting for me.\r\n\r\nWould you consider adding this feature to `mini.surround`?",
